#doc(title: [Physics: Forces and motion], subject: "Year 12 test")

// A paper written with the exam component (SPEC §13.1): the exam shows
// answer space where the mark scheme shows answers, mark codes and notes.

Answer *all* questions. The total mark for this paper is #exam.total-marks().

= Section A

#question[
  A ball is thrown vertically upwards at $12 "m/s"$. Take $g = 9.81 "m/s"^2$.

  #part(marks: 2)[
    Calculate the greatest height the ball reaches.
    #answer(lines: 3)[
      $h = u^2 / (2 g) = 7.3 "m"$ #mark("M1") #mark("A1")
    ]
  ]
  #part(marks: 3)[
    Calculate the time it takes to return to the thrower's hand.
    #answer(lines: 4)[
      $t = 2 u / g = 2.4 "s"$ #mark("M1") #mark("A1") #mark("A1")
      #markscheme-note[Accept 2.5 s from $g = 9.8 "m/s"^2$.]
    ]
  ]
] <q:ball>

#question(marks: 4)[
  A trolley of mass $2.0 "kg"$ is pushed along a smooth track. Its speed doubles from $1.5 "m/s"$ to $3.0 "m/s"$ in $4.0 "s"$.

  #part(marks: 2)[
    Find the resultant force on the trolley.
    #answer(lines: 3)[
      $F = m Delta v / t = 0.75 "N"$ #mark("M1") #mark("A1")
    ]
  ]
  #part[
    Find the work done on it.

    #part(marks: 1)[
      State the change in its kinetic energy.
      #answer(lines: 2)[$Delta E_k = 6.75 "J"$ #mark("B1")]
    ]
    #part(marks: 1)[
      Explain why it equals the work done.
      #answer(lines: 2)[The track is smooth, so no energy is transferred as heat. #mark("B1")]
    ]
  ]
]

= Section B

#question(marks: 1)[
  State Newton's third law of motion.
  #answer(lines: 2)[
    The forces two bodies exert on each other are equal and opposite. #mark("B1")
  ]
]

In @q:ball, the ball is a particle.
